    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW27wHwh6evB3MBjiu2K2XyU8)_\n\n## Merge order\n\n- Base: `main` (follow-up of #470, already merged); no other dependency.\n\n## Problem\n\n- After `d` (drop) in a report, the message of the command was shown for a moment and then replaced by the hints (\"the echo area blinks\").\n\n## Causes\n\n- **Duplicate forced call:** `sp-batch-report-open` had two extra `sp-echo-help-set` calls (one left over from #468 beside the one from #470). Each one forces the hints into the echo area, so every redraw (`d`, `u`, `g`) overwrote the message.\n- **Idle re-show too eager (my change in #470):** it replaced any message after the idle delay (1.5 s), so a message could not be read.\n\n## Changes\n\n- Removed the duplicate `sp-echo-help-set` call in `sp-batch-report-open`.\n- `sp-echo-help-set` has a new `QUIET` argument: the hints do not replace a message that is showing. A redraw (the point is put back) and the mode body set them quietly; opening a fresh report still shows them at once.\n- New `sp-echo-help-message-hold` (default 5 s): the idle re-show replaces a message only after Emacs has been idle that long. `C-c ?` still shows the hints at once.\n- Docs updated as bullets (`sp-interaction.org`, `sp-batch-report.org`); no CHANGELOG edit.\n\n## Tests (Emacs 29.3, batch)\n\n- `sp-batch-report-test` 22, `sp-echo-help-test` 7, `sp-async-work-test` 10 pass.\n- New `sp-batch-report-redraw-keeps-the-command-message`: redraw does not print the hints while a message is showing (this failed with the duplicate call); idle at 2 s leaves it, idle at 6 s shows the hints.\n- `sp-echo-help-idle-show-replaces-a-message` now checks the hold time.\n\n## Not tested by Claude\n\n- A real GUI session: I could not reproduce your exact \"Dropped\" message; the shared report code emits no such message itself, so it comes from the command you ran (a redraw or a `user-error`). Please check with the steps below.\n- The old (non-`sp-batch-report`) views (author notes old view, tag lint old view, graph view, litnote status) still force the hints on redraw; they were not changed.\n- The 5 s hold value is a guess; `sp-echo-help-message-hold` is a variable.\n\n## Manual testing\n\n- [ ] `cd ~/dotfiles; git fetch origin 476-echo-help-keep-messages; git checkout 476-echo-help-keep-messages`, restart Emacs (or `M-x sp-reload-modules`)\n- [ ] `M-x sp-author-notes`, then `d` on an entry: the message stays in the echo area (no blink); the hints return after 5 s idle or on the next command with an empty echo area\n- [ ] `d` on an already dropped entry (error message) and `u` on a non-dropped one: the message stays readable\n- [ ] `C-c ?` shows the hints at once, over any message\n- [ ] A fresh report (`M-x sp-litnotes-titles-dryrun`) shows the hints as soon as it opens\n- [ ] Other report/lint views (footnote lint, tag lint, graph view): note whether messages still get overwritten, and tell me which\n\n<details><summary>Revert after testing</summary>\n\n- `git -C ~/dotfiles status`, then `git -C ~/dotfiles restore .` for local edits.\n- `git -C ~/dotfiles switch main && git -C ~/dotfiles pull`, then restart Emacs or `M-x sp-reload-modules`.\n- Optionally `git -C ~/dotfiles branch -D 476-echo-help-keep-messages`.\n- The dry runs only read the vault; no vault restore needed.\n\n</details>\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNiCsjdfwKhDG3Nkddb7)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNiCsjdfwKhDG3Nkddb7\n",
